VERDICT: PROVEN
  OFF: two workers on one thread_id forked the checkpoint chain and left a
       message list holding a tool_result whose tool_use is on the other
       branch. Both workers reported success. Nothing logged a warning.
  ON:  the same zombie's writes were refused by Postgres, the chain did not
       fork, and the survivor's thread is intact and usable -- on both the
       pipeline path and the supports_pipeline=False fallback.
